 the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- **Data centres:** Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026, because power availability limits new sites. Demand is still rising, but the rate of increase is falling.\n- **Financing risk:** Conditions for utilities are tighter but not blocking. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably. Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. If equity funding stays weak, capital plans could be scaled back or delayed. I found no sign of that yet.\n\n**Limits:**\n- Only two sources, covering two utilities plus one data-centre figure.\n- The 2027 plans are the only forward data. I found nothing for 2026 itself or for 2028 onward.\n- These are planned budgets and connection requests, not placed equipment orders.\n- The utility capex documents don't say how much of the spending is driven by data centres.\n\nDetails are in n5.r1 (utilities) and n6.r1 (data centres).","ttft_ms":2416,"type":"result","duration_ms":36060,"uuid":"e1cc0fd1-f48c-48b0-8eff-07e554ed7269","ttft_stream_ms":1365,"time_to_request_ms":125,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":33,"input_hooks":5,"conversation_append":3,"transcript_persist":17,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":14,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":20,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":77,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":193,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":120,"process_rss_mib_result":200,"process_anon_mib_result":118,"process_peak_rss_mib":201,"process_cpu_ms_turn":655,"process_wall_ms_t